<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  NuGet sources of orkeon-studio-check (decision D17). Not the copy the templates share: the
  mapping differs.

  * orkeon-local : /usr/local/share/orkeon/packages, the feed the image builds (flat folder of
                   nupkg files). Two ids are taken from it, and only those:
                   - Orkeon.Studio.Core, packed from the Orkeon Studio sources by
                     scripts/build-orkeon-studio.sh at <OrkeonStudioVersion>; it is published nowhere;
                   - Orkeon.Compliance.Vfs, the analyzer, at <OrkeonVersion>, the version of the feed,
                     as in the templates.
  * nuget.org    : everything else, the two Orkeon packages Orkeon.Studio.Core depends on included:
                   `Orkeon` (the umbrella) and `Orkeon.Constants.Cli`, at the version that Studio
                   release pins in its own Directory.Packages.props (1.3.0 for Studio 1.3.0).

  Why those two come from nuget.org and not from the local feed: Studio builds against the published
  Orkeon packages, at one pinned version, and the umbrella `Orkeon` exists on nuget.org alone (the
  local feed holds the per-assembly packages, Orkeon.Domain and the others, never the umbrella). The
  local feed is at the version of the Orkeon the image installs, which is the pinned one only when
  that Orkeon is the release Studio pins: built from another commit of Orkeon (a source build, D32),
  the feed has another version and holds no Orkeon.Constants.Cli that Studio's pin accepts. Mapping
  the two ids to nuget.org works in both cases and keeps the check on the assemblies Studio ships
  with. A package source mapping takes the most specific pattern, so the two ids named under
  orkeon-local win over `*`, and no other Orkeon id can come from the local feed here.

  One id can then exist twice at one version: when the local feed is at the version Studio pins,
  Orkeon.Constants.Cli (and Orkeon.Compliance.Vfs) of that version are in the feed and on nuget.org,
  both built from the same tag. The package cache keeps the first one restored (the templates take
  theirs from the feed); the two hold the same constants.

  The clear element discards machine-level feeds. Verifying outside the image (feed in another
  directory): do not edit this file, run scripts/verify-templates.sh with its feed option.
-->
<configuration>
  <packageSources>
    <clear />
    <add key="nuget.org" value="https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json" />
    <add key="orkeon-local" value="/usr/local/share/orkeon/packages" />
  </packageSources>
  <packageSourceMapping>
    <packageSource key="orkeon-local">
      <package pattern="Orkeon.Studio.Core" />
      <package pattern="Orkeon.Compliance.Vfs" />
    </packageSource>
    <packageSource key="nuget.org">
      <package pattern="*" />
    </packageSource>
  </packageSourceMapping>
</configuration>
